WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.891
Lately, I have enjoyed sharing the gospel
this way. We should not be afraid to say

00:00:05.891 --> 00:00:06.780
these things.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:14.039
Two things happened in the past two weeks
that really encouraged me. Let me tell you

00:00:14.039 --> 00:00:14.900
about them.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.980
One of my MBA students was about to graduate
but had not found a job.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:27.700
They were very nervous, worried, and
anxious, so they came to talk to me.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.900
I took the opportunity to share the gospel
and said:

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.300
“I hope you will receive the Lord. But let
me say this first:

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.260
“Receiving the Lord and praying does not
guarantee that you will find a job.”

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.880
They said, “If it does not guarantee a job,
why should I pray?”

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.760
I said, “Do you think prayer is a
transaction? I am sorry,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.240
“God is not looking for people who want to
bargain with Him.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.120
“He is looking for people who want a
relationship with Him.”

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.120
“If you want a transaction, find someone
else. Do not make God your trading partner.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:13.220
“Why? You have no bargaining chips. What can
you give God?

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.877
“Anything you could give Him was first given
to you by Him. Even your life and breath

00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:22.540
are His gifts, which He can take back.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.140
“You have no bargaining chips that entitle
you to make a deal with God.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:33.060
“You started with nothing. Everything you
have was given to you by God.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.952
“If you treat Him like an ATM, you will find
that you never made a deposit. How can

00:01:38.952 --> 00:01:40.360
you withdraw anything?

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.085
“And God does not bargain with you. Why? He
has given you His very life. What more

00:01:46.085 --> 00:01:47.100
could He give you?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.320
“He has given His life to you and me. What
is left for Him to bargain over?

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.920
“So if you want to make a deal with God,
there is nothing more to discuss.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:03.000
“But if you want to know God and have a
relationship with Him, we can keep talking.”

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:10.190
Do you know what they did? They confessed
and said, “I am sorry.

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.990
“I had this bargaining attitude. But I do
want a relationship with God.”

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.710
We led them in prayer, and they received the
Lord.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:27.230
They asked, “Where can I buy a Bible?” I
said, “No problem. We will give you one.”

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.130
They wanted to start reading it.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.480
I believe we need not be afraid to share the
gospel this way.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.640
If someone really wants to bargain with God,
it will not work. It is better to tell

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.720
them that early.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:49.460
That is not our business. We introduce
people to a loving relationship with God.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.720
If they want to love God, we can make the
introduction.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.380
But if they want to trade with God, they
should go work at a stock exchange!
